WEBVTT

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.140
Doctor, what's that smell?

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.070
You can smell it?

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.230
It's odorless to ordinary people.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.560
Which means...

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.750
Yep. The smell attracts the mysterious.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.750
People infected by the mysterious 
are unconsciously drawn to it.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.990
We're not fishing for eels, here.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.190
Excuse me.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.590
I'm sorry.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.860
It's like my body led me here.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.270
<i>Someone actually came.</i>

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:11.360
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.990
<b>Episode 4 "Chili Pepper Fingertips"</b>

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.670
Your fingertips turned into chili peppers?

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.480
I've tried cutting and breaking them 
off, but they're hard and it hurts.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.300
Have you tried boiling them?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.860
Doctor, don't be ridiculous.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.740
Boiling them didn't work.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.250
It didn't work, huh?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.490
<i>You actually boiled them?</i>

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.560
A mysterious disease that 
infects your fingernails, huh?

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.880
Mysterious disease?

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:42.370
Mysterious diseases are the weird illnesses 
you get when you're infected by the mysterious.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:47.170
They strike when your body and mind 
are off balance due to stress.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.820
Stress?

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.690
Looks like you have some idea 
about what's causing it.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.460
But don't worry.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:06.450
Mysterious Disease Specialist 
Dr. Ramune will cure you.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.650
Kuro.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.200
Yes.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.840
Purple shelf, top row.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.370
Bring me what's inside the 
second drawer from the right.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.910
I'll lend you these.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.070
Nail clippers for mysterious diseases.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.600
These are nail clippers?

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.340
Yeah, they're inside the bag.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:31.220
Fingernails have always been vulnerable 
to the mysterious and fox spirits.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.100
That's why there's a relatively large 
number of tools for driving them off.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.210
But among them, this one's exceptional.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:42.110
You should have no trouble 
removing your chili peppers.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.930
They're that powerful?

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.300
Huh? The knot's too tight.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.050
I can't untie it.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.540
Yeah. Those clippers are as 
proud as they are strong.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:57.540
They choose their users, so 
not many people can use them.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.620
Then I won't be able to use them.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.920
Now, now. Imagine you're being 
interviewed and hold on to them.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.050
Interviewed?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:10.490
Who are you, and what are you capable of?

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.320
Hide nothing. Lay it all out there.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.140
Once they deem you worthy of using them,

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.040
the knot will come undone.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.920
You're being rather hands-off again.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.530
It's fine to leave guys who 
grow chili peppers alone.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.580
And besides, he realized 
the cause on his own.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:43.320
If he can figure that out himself, 
he can cure himself.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:47.580
That is, if he feels like it.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:50.960
Good morning.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.920
Bungo-kun, good morning.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.330
Hey, Bungo.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.770
Good morning.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.350
Good morning.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.130
Bungo-kun is so cool.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.480
He's the track team's ace, and 
he's got a handsome face.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.120
Takaharu, good morning.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.380
Good morning.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.230
Bungo-kun is so nice.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.000
He's even talking to Plain Old Haru.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>Faculty Office</b>

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.990
Uh, sir.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.110
What did you want to discuss?

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.140
It's about the test you took the other day.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.350
Th-The test?

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:28.260
Takaharu, why did you write 
wrong answers on purpose?

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:34.710
You finished the test faster 
than anyone else in the class.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.760
But then you rewrote your answers.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.110
See? Right here.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.730
I can see the correct answer you 
erased under the wrong answer.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:52.770
In any case, regardless of the 
reason, don't do it again.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.830
S-Sorry...

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.460
11.5 seconds.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.900
Bungo, you're so fast. Of course 
you're on the track team.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:12.390
Running in sneakers on a dirt 
field really does slow me down.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.420
You're still plenty fast, though!

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.440
12.1 seconds.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.620
No way. Seriously?

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.070
Plain Old Haru's pretty fast.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:25.160
Crap, I lost to Plain Old Haru!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.160
What?

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:29.170
<i>Crap. That still qualifies as fast?</i>

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.100
Bungo, did you see that?

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.230
Plain Old Haru's fast.

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.100
Surprising skill for him, huh?

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.400
Not really.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.820
He's totally slow.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.560
I knew it.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.560
They're not prescription. Fake glasses, huh?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.130
Bungo.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.900
What was with your 100-meter time just now?

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.280
What do you mean?

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.210
I ran unexpectedly fast.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.880
I surprised even myself.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.350
What?

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.880
Oh, Bungo-kun!

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.220
Oh, my god. Who are you?

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:12.650
Huh?

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.910
It's Takaharu.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.000
What? Plain Old Haru?

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.140
No way. He's so hot!

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.740
I don't believe it!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.410
I see.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:28.050
Doctor, the pot is boiling.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:28.950
Whoa!

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.300
I'll help.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.890
Could you pass me that?

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.390
<b>Hawk Talon Chili Peppers</b>

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.480
Oh...

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.140
Let's eat.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.320
They say a skilled hawk hides his talons,

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.460
but pretending you can't do what you 
can causes stress, don't you think?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.650
That must be what the mysterious 
latched on to this time.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.230
Because he suppressed and hid himself,

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:59.910
his fingernails turned into chili peppers.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.540
It's true.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.030
Plain Old Haru is really hot 
when he takes off his glasses.

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.650
Seriously?

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:08.730
Who's hotter, Bungo-kun or him?

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.050
Honestly, probably Plain Old Haru.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.680
Take your seats!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.550
It's time for a quiz.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.400
Looks like you're finished.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.940
I'll hold on to this.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.390
I'm returning your quizzes!

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.220
Takaharu, full marks.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.240
Here's yours, Bungo.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.340
Yes, sir.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.710
You were close.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.050
What? Full marks? Wow.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:52.140
Takaharu, you're smart, too?

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.850
Hey, take off your glasses.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.090
<i>The knot's looser?</i>

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:04.520
<i>Why?</i>

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.940
Who are you, and what are you capable of?

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.380
Hide nothing. Lay it all out there.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.670
<i>Is it because I couldn't hide it?</i>

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.660
Akatsuki

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:27.720
Really? There's a boy who might be able 
to use the Purse's Nail Clippers?

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:29.170
How unusual.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.160
I'd love to see that.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:36.930
You said those nail clippers 
choose their users.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.170
Will he be able to use them?

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.710
He grew chili peppers, right?

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.550
Then it's a possibility.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:44.530
What?

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:48.570
In the first place, that type of 
mysterious affliction won't come near people

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:50.860
unless they're exceptionally talented.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:51.950
I see...

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:56.940
Thanks for the food!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.460
Delicious!

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:07.660
If he's so talented, why 
does he bother hiding it?

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:13.410
For something, or some<i>one</i>.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:14.360
What?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:20.790
They say human relationships 
are the cause of most stress.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:27.050
Because no man is an island,

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:30.080
people feel joy and sadness 
especially keenly.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:35.690
<i>If I reveal who I am, the 
knot will come undone.</i>

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.690
<i>I'll be cured of these weird fingernails.</i>

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:52.570
<i>But then, Bungo would go back to being...</i>

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.460
57th 
<b><i>All-Japan Middle School Track and Field Tournament
 </i></b>108th Track and Field Championship Relay

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:02.160
<i>We were always friends and rivals.</i>

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:09.600
<i>The winner of the middle school boys' 
100 meter is Otomo Takaharu-kun.</i>

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.050
You're amazing, Takaharu.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:15.100
I'm glad to have raced against you.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.830
Bungo, let's go cool do—

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:35.950
Bungo, you like Chiharu-chan?

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.960
How surprising.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.580
You got a problem with that?

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:42.470
No, you guys would make a great couple.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:46.510
Takaharu-kun, I like you.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.210
We'll be together in high school, too.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.280
Yeah. I'll apply to the 
same high school as you.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.280
Academic Achievement Test 

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:05.160
I knew you'd get in on a 
recommendation, Takaharu.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:08.790
It's okay. I'll take the entrance exam.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:11.680
Come on. Share, you two.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:14.090
Aw, man.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.790
If I didn't have a brother, 
it would be all mine.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:21.330
<i>That's right. If I weren't around...</i>

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:26.060
<i>If I hid myself, Bungo 
could have everything.</i>

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.050
<i>At least, that's how it was supposed to be.</i>

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:38.740
Takaharu.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.130
Want to walk home together?

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.030
Doctor.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:01.540
Those look terrible on you. 
I'm confiscating them.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:09.060
Hey, is this my fault?

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:13.060
The glasses, the tests, the 100-meter race.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.440
Is this all my fault, Takaharu?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.790
Are you trying to be considerate of me?

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.350
N-No, I—

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.570
Why won't you join the track team?

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:28.130
I placed first for the first 
time at our last track meet.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:31.310
Until now, it had always been you.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:35.330
But I wasn't even a little happy about it.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:40.160
I'm always thinking, "Takaharu 
would've run like this."

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.270
"How would Takaharu have 
solved this problem?"

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:47.460
I'm always chasing the illusion of you 
from when you were better than me.

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:51.750
So please, Takaharu.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.260
I don't want an illusion.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:14:00.200
I want to fight the real you 
fair and square and win.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.850
You've already won, then.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.720
You're an amazing guy.

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:14.390
Everyone in our class likes you.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:15.780
You should be confident.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.710
Are you serious?

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.660
I thought you were my friend.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:26.980
I thought we were rivals.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.970
I thought we'd always be equals.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:33.820
What do you really think of me, huh?!

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:37.720
Bungo!

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:43.230
Race me in a 100-meter dash 
tomorrow after school.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.980
If you hold back or refuse to race me,

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:51.810
I'll never talk to you again!

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:57.580
Whoa, is he crying?

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.440
<b>Okonomiyaki & Teppanyaki</b>

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:05.130
<b>Topology</b>

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:05.710
I see.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.750
You're such an awkward idiot.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:17.640
In the first place, you're shouldn't have
 brought pity into a competition.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:21.120
If you win, even if your opponents 
are crying in frustration,

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.390
you should celebrate and 
take pride in your victory.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:28.400
It's the highest praise you 
can offer your opponents.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:33.470
But you went with, "I feel bad that he 
lost, so I'll hold back next time."

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.130
"I'll even let him win."

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.030
You've gone way beyond rude.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:42.740
That wasn't my intention.

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:46.500
Even if it wasn't your intention, 
that's how he sees it.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:49.980
What should I do?

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:53.240
What should I say to Bungo?

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:54.520
Who knows?

00:15:55.530 --> 00:16:00.870
But whether your friendship ends and
 you still have those weird fingernails,

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:05.510
or you make up with him 
and possibly cure them,

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:10.400
depends on how you respond to the challenge 
you've been issued tomorrow, doesn't it?

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.380
Midterm Exams

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:38.010
Bungo.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:42.550
Good morning.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.050
Good morning...

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.140
Takaharu, your glasses...

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.050
Just so you know,

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.100
I won't lose.

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:59.080
Neither will I!

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:09.420
All right. This allows us to sneak 
in without seeming out of place.

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.100
What is that?

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:13.160
It's a blond thug.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.180
You are <i>completely</i> out of place.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.230
The rules are simple.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:21.860
Whoever crosses the 100-meter line first wins.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.330
I'll fire the starting pistol.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.780
Fine, but... who are you?

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:30.690
Oh, you know. Yamada from Class 3.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.700
Is there someone like that in that class?

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.690
How many years has it been 
since I last held a gun?

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:39.770
Doctor, I'll go watch the finish line.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:46.840
We haven't raced together since 
the finals at nationals.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.850
This is kind of crazy. I'm pretty nervous.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:53.260
Me, too.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:54.830
On your marks.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:58.750
Set.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:07.120
<i>Who are you, and what are you capable of?</i>

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:09.620
<i>Hide nothing. Lay it all out there.</i>

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.870
<i>I won't hide anymore.</i>

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.410
All right!

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.470
Damn, I lost.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.520
You idiot. No way I'd lose to someone 
who's been taking a break.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:18:59.780
What is this?

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.530
I'm frustrated and angry that I lost,

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:06.650
but I love running with you.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:13.020
So do I, idiot.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.800
<b>Changing Room 1</b>

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:16.800
A skilled hawk hides his talons,

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:20.130
but they'll grow dull if 
he keeps them hidden forever.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.790
From now on, you'd better keep them sharp.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.340
Will it come untied when I lost?

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.840
Who knows?

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:30.930
But if you laid it all out there 
instead of hiding yourself,

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:32.980
it'll probably come undone.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.330
It opened.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:42.610
Wow! These are the Purse's Nail Clippers?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.940
Doctor, is this your first time seeing them?

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:47.150
Didn't I tell you?

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.880
Not many people can use them!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.290
I-It came off.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:14.060
Are you sure that's all 
you wanted as payment?

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:17.590
Well, I didn't do anything this time.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:20.010
If anything, this is more than I deserve.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.270
Here. You can have one.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:27.060
They're chili peppers coated with 
the power of the nail clippers.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:30.350
Simply having one on you will drive 
away some of the mysterious.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.880
<i>Did he choose that treatment 
method because he wanted these?</i>

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:38.590
Doctor, who is he?

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:39.870
Huh?

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:45.880
Those nail clippers went back inside 
the bag when you touched them.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:49.380
How did he use a mysterious 
item not even you can—

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:51.210
Kuro, let's go home.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:06.870
<b>The Purse's Nail Clippers</b>

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:13.410
"The Purse's Nail Clippers are a powerful, 
first-class mysterious item.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:17.150
However, they love handsome 
faces and are extremely picky.

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:22.240
They can only be used by men who 
possess a handsome appearance,

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:27.190
great intelligence, a noble 
character, and tremendous talent."

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:32.680
Appearance

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:32.680
Intelligence & Character

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.430
Handsome, intelligent, and noble.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.460
Bungo, let's go to practice.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:41.320
Yeah.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:44.560
Well? Think you can come 
back from your break?

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:47.810
Yeah. I'll pass you before long.

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:48.950
Now you've said it.

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:29.130
<i>Our next patient's ears 
have turned into pot stickers.</i>

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:31.690
<i>Boiled or fried?</i>

00:23:31.690 --> 00:23:34.200
<i>Does that matter for the treatment?</i>

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:36.070
Dr. Ramune -Mysterious Disease Specialist-.

00:23:36.070 --> 00:23:38.970
